WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.934
-Welcome back to the show, and
congrats on getting married.

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:04.133
-Yes.
-This is a big deal.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:06.801
It happened.
-Yep.

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:09.367
-This Thursday, you'll
be able to see the wedding

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:11.934
in the two-part finale
of "Paris in Love."

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:14.434
I have some photos here to show.

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:17.300
This is beautiful.
This is you at the altar.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.367
-Yes.
-Gorgeous.

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:20.033
-I love that
Oscar de la Renta gown.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:21.501
-Wowzers.

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:23.934
This is you and Carter
walking down the aisle.

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.601
-Mm-hmm.
-Look at this.

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:28.734
How was it? How was everything?

00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:30.934
What went wrong?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:32.901
Something always goes
wrong at a wedding.

00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:34.767
-It was magical.
It was everything.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.968
I think the only thing I was
stressing out about was,

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:38.334
I hadn't written my vows

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:40.434
up until I was literally
about to walk down the aisle.

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:43.334
I was, like, rushing.
It was very stressful.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:47.000
That's a lot of pressure.
Do you remember what you said?

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.667
-I just ended up throwing them
on the floor during my speech

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.334
and then just started speaking
from the heart.

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:54.934
So it went way better.
-Wow. Did you get emotional?

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.968
-He was crying
the entire time.

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:58.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:02.634
I was like, "I am not ruining
this mascara and my gown,"

00:01:02.634 --> 00:01:04.467
so I held it in.
-That's so funny.

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:06.400
Last time we talked, you said
you were gonna

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.133
make 10 outfit changes.
Did you?

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:10.801
-I wanted to live up to that,
but I only did seven.

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:12.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:13.801
-But you did do it.
-Yeah.

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:16.033
-Was it tough to do,
to keep going and changing?

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:18.734
-Sort of.
It would have been tougher

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:21.267
to do at the Santa Monica Pier
for the Neon Carnival

00:01:21.267 --> 00:01:22.634
because there's
nowhere to change.

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:24.501
But we had the wedding
at my grandfather's old estate,

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:27.033
so I just got dressed
in my old teenage room.

00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:28.834
It was cute.
-Wow.

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:31.634
How about first dance?
Was that good, stress you out?

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:34.133
-That was the one thing
I was dreading,

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:35.834
because I hate ballroom dancing.

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:38.667
I'm good at, like, raving
and jumping around.

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:40.801
But, like, a fancy dance --
-Yeah, you can't do that.

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:44.167
-I was like, "I can't."
But I killed that, too.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:48.200
-Oh, my gosh. You're ridiculous.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.100
So funny.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.000
Can you tell us
your first-dance song?

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.200
-Bruno Mars,
"Just the Way You Are."

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.934
-Aww.
-I love that song.

00:01:57.934 --> 00:02:00.968
-Did you have any other song
under consideration?

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:04.000
-"Stars Are Blind," my song.
-Yeah!

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.067
-But Kim Petras sang it.
-That would have been great.

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:08.167
-She already sang it --
Kim Petras is my friend --

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:09.834
sand it as I was walking
down the aisle.

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.667
-She did?
-Yes.

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:14.133
-I ran into your mom,
by the way, who's super cute

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:15.834
and awesome and funny,
and she told me

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:17.834
that Demi Lovato crushed it.

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:20.400
-Oh, my God,
that was just so beautiful,

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.133
singing
"I Will Always Love You."

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:25.133
Everybody was crying.
-Demi Lovato is legit.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:27.601
-So talented.
-I mean, pipes.

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:29.300
Yeah! Oh, that's so fun.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:30.567
How was your mom
during the wedding?

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:33.601
-She was a lot of fun.
My mom --

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:35.667
No one knows how to throw
a party like my mom.

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:37.901
That's where I get it from.
-She seems fun.

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:39.767
-Yeah, she's so cool.
She loves you.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:45.400
-She's great.
Also she's just a character.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.634
She's so fun.
I mean, she's

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:48.300
the best thing on television.
-Thank you.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.033
-I think she's
the funniest person.

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:52.067
I want to show everyone
a clip of your show.

00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:54.234
This is Paris finding
wedding inspiration

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:56.334
in the craziest --
Where is this place?

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:59.334
-Las Vegas, Area15.
It's like an indoor Burning Man.

00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:02.000
It's sick.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.868
-This is real.
Take a look at this.

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:06.267
-I've been going to Burning Man
for the past 10 years.

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:08.567
It's one of my favorite events.

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:11.300
It's so magical, and
it's like nothing on earth.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:14.167
And Area15 is like
an indoor Burning Man.

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:16.734
So I thought, what a better way
to kick off the weekend?

00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:20.467
No, I don't want to race.

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:22.501
-Oh!

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.067
♪♪

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:26.501
-Oh, babe, wait for me.

00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:28.133
-Yes!

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.067
Oh, yes!

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:32.033
-It pays to go with
Paris Hilton to Vegas,

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:34.100
'cause they treat you
like the queen.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.434
[ Both chuckle ]

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:38.100
-What is that?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.400
-It's amazing. You have to go.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.267
-I have to go to that place.

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:46.434
Last time you were on the show,
I asked you to explain NFTs.

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:49.834
And you did so in a great way,
which is a very hard thing

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:51.767
to really explain
to a lot of people.

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:53.534
But since then, "Forbes"
has named you

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:57.501
one of the top 50
most influential people

00:03:57.501 --> 00:03:59.968
in the NFT space.
So congrats on that.

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:03.634
-Thank you.
Thank you. I'm so proud.

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:04.968
I love being
part of this community

00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:06.868
and being a voice and
sharing my platform

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:08.100
and just getting the word
out there,

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.300
because I think it's just
such an incredible thing

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.634
to be a part of.
-Yeah, I jumped in.

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:13.868
-I know, I heard.

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.501
I'm so happy
I taught you what they were.

00:04:15.501 --> 00:04:16.734
-You did.
You taught me what's up.

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:19.234
And then I bought an ape.
-I got an ape, too,

00:04:19.234 --> 00:04:21.167
because I saw you on the show
with Beeple,

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:22.467
and you got on Moonpay,

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:24.300
so I went and I copied you
and did the same thing.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.534
-You did?
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:29.701
-This is your ape.
-Yeah, it's really cool.

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:31.601
Look at the hat, the shades.

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:36.367
-How did you pick --
because you can pick your ape.

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:38.267
-Yes. I was going through
a lot of them.

00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:39.534
And I was like,
"I want something

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:41.634
that kind of reminds me of me,"

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:44.734
but this one, it does.

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:47.767
I think we made, like,
another version of it,

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:50.734
where he takes the hat off
and blond hair comes out.

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:53.334
-Ah, 'cause you can do now
whatever you want.

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:57.033
-Mm-hmm. Animated version.
-We're part of the community.

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:58.634
We're both apes.
-I love it.

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:00.667
-Here's my ape. This is my ape.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.567
-Yours is so cool.

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:05.100
I love the red heart sunglasses.
I love the captain hat.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.834
-It reminded me of me
a little bit,

00:05:06.834 --> 00:05:09.267
because I wear striped shirts.
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:11.200
I've worn
these heart sunglasses,

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.267
'cause my daughters,
just as a joke --

00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:15.400
they have them, and as a joke,
I've put them on.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.000
So, I've done this.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.033
And I love Yacht Rock
and being breezy.

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:21.801
So I'm like, "Yeah."
And I like the blue.

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:23.400
-Mm-hmm.
-Dude, look at this.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.901
-They looks like
they could be
friends.

00:05:24.901 --> 00:05:27.200
-They're buddies.
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:28.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.601 --> 00:05:31.100
But this is --
you have a new NFT.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.767
You have one
being released soon.

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:36.801
We have it here.
What can you tell us about this?

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:40.467
-Well, it's an NFT series
I'm doing with Superplastic.

00:05:40.467 --> 00:05:42.400
And we're releasing
on Origin Protocol.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.334
And then I made
another piece by hand.

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:48.067
Took me six months.
And it's a collage

00:05:48.067 --> 00:05:50.601
of all of my memories
with Carter.

00:05:50.601 --> 00:05:53.000
And it's called
"My Forever Fairytale."

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.267
-Wow.
And here's the actual collage.

00:05:55.267 --> 00:05:58.868
-Yes.
-This is big.

00:05:58.868 --> 00:06:00.267
I think people
are gonna love this.

00:06:00.267 --> 00:06:02.434
-Well, if you love it so much,

00:06:02.434 --> 00:06:04.234
I actually want to give you
the first one.

00:06:04.234 --> 00:06:06.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:08.334
Mm-hmm.
-I would be honored.

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:10.167
-And I want to give one
to everyone in the audience.

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:11.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:11.767 --> 00:06:14.100
-Everyone gets an NFT?
-Yes, everyone.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.033
-Everyone gets an NFT tonight!
Paris!

00:06:17.033 --> 00:06:19.234
Come on!
I think that's

00:06:19.234 --> 00:06:21.934
the NFT giveaway
in television history.

00:06:21.934 --> 00:06:23.033
We love you!
-Iconic!

00:06:23.033 --> 00:06:24.767
-Paris Hilton!
Who else does that?

00:06:24.767 --> 00:06:25.901
-Love you guys.
-Paris and I

00:06:25.901 --> 00:06:27.667
will do something fun
after the break.

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:29.300
We have a very special guest
to help us out.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.467
Stick around.
For real? We all get them?

